        "subject": "LU-19455 tests: avoid list statahead in sanity 123h",
        "message": "LU-19455 tests: avoid list statahead in sanity 123h\n\ntest_123h can fail with \"hit total is too low\" at about 1 run in\n2000. When the lowest numbered file name also happens to be the\nfirst entry in readdir (hash) order, which differs on every\nfilesystem, statahead detects the directory listing pattern on\nthe first stat() instead of the file name pattern. It then\nprefetches in hash order while the test walks the names in\nnumeric order, so almost every lookup misses.\n\nRemove such an entry before the scan so the file name pattern\nis the only one that can match.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I4615f1cf0e57db1b26ff5f4fd7d30c678f65cf6c\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
